From: =?UTF-8?q?S=C3=B6nke=20Liebau?= <soenke.liebau@stackable.tech>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 11:25:25 +0000
Subject: Rewrite DB2-style DECODE into CASE in the parser

DECODE(e, s1, r1, s2, r2, ..., [default]) is rewritten to
CASE e WHEN IS NOT DISTINCT FROM s1 THEN r1 ... ELSE default END,
so a NULL operand matches a NULL search value and the operand is
evaluated once. The rewrite happens before analysis, so calls with
more than 127 arguments work.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
